      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. they're a good start. \n\ni feel like the traditionalist one is almost *too* calm, like he's a saint or something. and the progressive one feels a bit like a caricature of someone just yelling for the sake of it.\n\ncan we try again? i want them to actually argue about a specific local issue, like the town council trying to rezoning the historic district for high-density affordable housing. \n\ncan u rewrite the monologues so they're both making a point about that? try to make them both sound like they have a really valid, logical reason for what they want, even if the progressive is still more high-energy/intense.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
